  "query_preview": ".. \n(Today through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Trough energy approaches Nevada from the\nPacific Northwest today with the main impact being an increase in\nwinds this afternoon. Most locations can expect sustained W to SW\nwinds of 10 to 15 mph with gusts of 15 to 25 mph this afternoon\nand early evening. High temperatures this afternoon will remain \nwell above normal with most areas seeing a near repeat of \nyesterday's highs. \n\nMajor changes in the weather this weekend as cooler trough energy\ndropping in from the Pac NW helps to draw a very moist air mass \nup through southern California and into central and eastern \nNevada. There is a marginal risk of excessive rainfall Sunday into\nMonday. The driest portion of the CWA Sunday and Monday will be \nHumboldt County where storm total precipitation is expected to \nrange from around a tenth of an inch in the far NW corner of the \ncounty, to around a quarter to a third of an inch over the Santa \nRosa mts and the Winnemucca area, up to around a half inch in the\nSE corner of the county near Valmy. \n\nMuch wetter conditions are expected for the remainder of the CWA \nfrom Sunday morning through Monday night. Most valley locations \nacross Elko, Lander, Eureka and N Nye County can expect at least \na half inch of rain between Sunday morning and Tuesday morning \nwith an inch or more in the mountains. Even heavier rainfall \namounts are expected across east-central NV, including the \nsouthern portion of Elko County, all of White Pine County and \nportions of NE Nye County where valley locations could easily \nreceive an inch or more of rainfall. Rainfall could be heavy at\ntimes. A Flood Watch may be required. Ponding of water is likely \nin many areas later this weekend into early next week, with \nadditional concern for debris flows across recent burn scars.\n\nThe upper level low/trough centered over the Pac NW Saturday\nmorning will gradually dig south across western California through\nthe weekend. By Monday evening the system will be centered over \nsouthern CA, then eject eastward through southern NV and into the \nfour corners region by late Tuesday. Lighter rain showers are \nexpected to continue over most of northern and central Nevada \nMonday night into Tuesday morning with showers ending from west to\neast Tuesday afternoon and overnight. Dry but noticeably cooler \nconditions are expected Wednesday through at least next Friday. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence in\nunseasonably warm temperatures this afternoon. High forecast \nconfidence regarding strong wind gusts in Central Nevada Saturday \nand Sunday. High forecast confidence regarding significant \nrainfall in Eastern Nevada Sunday into Monday. High forecast \nconfidence in a cooling trend Saturday through Monday.",
